   "innovation": "Semi-causal language modeling: autoregressively generates tokens while some spans are represented by bidirectional encoders, enabling the model to process the whole session from left to right while leveraging bidirectional context for specific spans; Universal task layer docking: a unidirectional Transformer decoder acts as a general-purpose interface that docks with multiple bidirectional encoders via a connector layer, allowing natural language to serve as a programming language for underlying pretrained models; Multi-turn conversational support: natively supports multi-turn interactions by feeding encoded inputs to the interface layer and generating responses in a semi-causal manner, combining in-context learning and open-ended generation. Differs from standard causal LMs by incorporating bidirectional encoders for specific spans, and from encoder-decoder architectures by using a single unidirectional decoder as a universal task layer.",
